   "class": "deviation",
   "fix": "Replace \"No cell is in both sets.\" with \"A cell is in both sets only when a component's stage-1 port is wired back to its own input; the two gathers then read the same table value.\"",
   "note": "The conclusion that y and u carry no freshness distinction still holds. Only the absolute claim fails. I found no spec line that forbids a stage-1 self-wire."
  },
  {
   "id": "K6a-069",
   "file": "design/companions/event_visibility_walkthrough.md",
   "line": 182,
   "kind": "mech",
   "claim": "The executor builds each handler's bundle exactly as it builds every other bundle",
   "evidence": "src/executor.jl:236-242 builds the handler bundle with `gather_input_barrier`, a @noinline wrapper (src/store.jl:100). The stage, RHS and guard bundles gather inline (executor.jl:128-146). Only the update entry shares the handler's barrier.",
   "verdict": "finding",
   "class": "drift",
   "fix": "Replace \"exactly as it builds every other bundle\" with \"as it builds every other bundle, the update entry's included, with the gather behind a function barrier\".",
   "note": "Semantics are the same: the gather reads the live table and allocates nothing (probe:80 gives 0). The barrier is an escape-analysis device, recorded in design/reports/20261106_update_entry_escape_analysis/report.md."
  }
